From 91b4e0eeafaff7b0f431210345f82bc4a2735f35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:43:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(view): keep the anchored edges of a float when the client
 resizes it

A floating window placed by a position rule grew from its top-left corner
no matter which anchor the rule named, so a right-anchored window that
widened for a side panel ran off the screen. The edges the anchor names
now stay put when the client changes its size: a right window grows to
the left, a centered one both ways.

Upstream-Status: Pending
